{"availability":"available","full":"jaypetez/jaypetez.github.io","name":"jaypetez.github.io","description":"My personal site and blog — Astro, zero framework JS, and a test suite that enforces the design system","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-31T17:47:11Z","updated":"2026-10-08T19:17:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jaypetez.github.io/","topics":["accessibility","astro","blog","github-pages","personal-website","static-site","typescript"],"demo":"https://jaypetez.github.io/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.543Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.543Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.543Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.543Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Built with Astro, no client-side framework, and about 1.5 KB of JavaScript on the wire. Static HTML, self-hosted fonts, and a design system that a test suite keeps honest.","The reference points are plain-text engineering artifacts: RFC figures, ls -l column alignment, the man page. One rule holds it together — structure (names, labels, dates, navigation) is monospace, prose is serif — and one ornament spends the whole decoration budget: the hand-aligned ASCII diagram of the stack on the home page, which is also a map of the projects listed under it. The palette is a two-colour printer ribbon: ink on paper, with the red band as the single accent; links in running text are ink with a red hairline under them, so a paragraph of citations reads as text first.","The layout is a ledger, not a grid of cards. Dates sit in a fixed-width gutter so every title starts on the same column, and on a wide screen the right margin does work instead of sitting empty: the stack figure sits beside the name on the home page, and each essay gets a numbered table of contents that sticks beside the text (its numbers and the section numbers come from the same CSS counter, so they cannot disagree). On a phone all of it stacks back into one column. None of this needs JavaScript."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jaypetez/jaypetez.github.io/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d9d99ca755c21d57fe94e8ba09406ac1c7acaa095d5c3133614b80f1e5bb5343","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.630Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.630Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Built with Astro, no client-side framework, and about 1.5 KB of JavaScript on the wire. Static HTML, self-hosted fonts, and a design system that a test suite keeps honest.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jaypetez/jaypetez.github.io/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d9d99ca755c21d57fe94e8ba09406ac1c7acaa095d5c3133614b80f1e5bb5343","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jaypetez/jaypetez.github.io/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.630Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T19:17:05Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jaypetez/jaypetez.github.io/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:24.631Z","hash":"d9d99ca755c21d57fe94e8ba09406ac1c7acaa095d5c3133614b80f1e5bb5343","originalBytes":6730,"storedBytes":6730,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["tests","build","content","license","src","astro","every","link","mit","one","page","project","title","because","code","components","contributing.md","deployment","description","design","draft","github","hosted","it.","post","rather","real","schema","site","source","two","which","above","accessibility","actions","adding","allowed","anti-slop","any","api","aria-current","assert","asserting","axe","before","between","blog","border-radius","both","branch","broken.","budget.","channel","characters","ci.yml","code.","collaborators","comments","concrete","configuration","configured","constraints","container","content.config.ts","contract","contrast","contributed","contributing","credit","data","dat